<title>NETHERLANDS: ABN acquires Indosuez assets in Sri Lanka.</title>
<headline>ABN acquires Indosuez assets in Sri Lanka.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1996-11-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch bank ABN AMRO Holding NV said on Thursday it had agreed to acquire the assets and liabilities of Banque Indosuez in Sri Lanka.</p>
<p>&quot;The acquisition follows the decision of Banque Indosuez to stop its commercial activities in Sri Lanka,&quot; ABN AMRO said.</p>
<p>ABN AMRO, which already had an office of its own in Sri Lanka, said it was acquiring assets worth 105 million guilders but gave no further details of the deal.</p>
<p>Banque Indosuez will retain a presence in Sri Lanka through its participation in Asia Capital Limited.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000</p>
